.TH ORO-DOCUMENT-ACCESS 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:document\-access \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:document\-access'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Persistent Android Storage Access Framework grants for user\-selected URIs. Providers can revoke grants or refuse persistence; callers must handle errors.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBlist()\fR
Lists persisted grants. This does not establish that the provider is reachable. Other platforms reject with `ENOSYS`.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DocumentGrant[]>\fR
.TP
\fBpersist(uri, options)\fR
Retains an existing user\-selected document grant across process death/reboot. Android must have granted the requested persistable modes; this never opens a permission prompt or obtains access to an arbitrary URI. At most 128 grants.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIuri\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (DocumentGrantOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBrelease(uri, options)\fR
Releases retained access. Close open files and stop using the URI first.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIuri\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (DocumentGrantOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
.TP
\fBstat(uri)\fR
Queries a selected document or tree root without resolving a filesystem path. Unknown provider sizes remain null. Queries have a five\-second result deadline; a timed\-out provider may still occupy one of the two bounded worker slots. Providers enforce existing grants. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIuri\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DocumentMetadata>\fR
.TP
\fBreadDirectory(uri, options)\fR
Lists children within an existing selected tree grant. Entries contain proper child document URIs. Pages follow provider cursor order, which is not a durable snapshot: after edits or process loss, restart and reconcile by URI. At most 128 entries and 1 MiB of metadata per response, with two concurrent queries. This does not broaden grants or emulate ordinary filesystem path traversal. Other platforms reject with ENOSYS.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIuri\fR (string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (DocumentChildrenOptions; optional)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DocumentChildren>\fR
